1: //! A slice of the void-claim telemetry subsystem.
2: //!
3: //! `series` is the shared ring buffer every sensor channel writes into. Each
4: //! `chan_*` module owns one channel: it decides what a sample means, what counts
5: //! as a spike for that channel, and how the dashboard should label it.
6: //!
7: //! The channels are independent by design -- a pressure sensor and a thermal
8: //! sensor have nothing to say to each other -- so each one grew its own copy of
9: //! the windowed-aggregate walk over the series it owns.
10: 
11: pub mod series;
12: 
13: pub mod chan_ambient;
14: pub mod chan_comms;
15: pub mod chan_coolant;
16: pub mod chan_cryo;
17: pub mod chan_dock;
18: pub mod chan_gyro;
19: pub mod chan_hull;
20: pub mod chan_optics;
21: pub mod chan_power;
22: pub mod chan_reactor;
23: pub mod chan_thruster;
24: pub mod chan_vent;
25: 
26: /// One reading, as the sensor bus delivers it.
27: #[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq)]
28: pub struct Sample {
29:     /// Milliseconds since the run began.
